{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And the man shall be clear of iniquity.</b> Even though he suspected a worthy woman, for she brought it upon herself by transgressing his warning and created grounds for suspicion, as they said, may their memory be for blessing (Shabbat 56a): 'David did not accept slander, for he saw recognizable signs in Mephibosheth.'" "<b>And that woman shall bear her iniquity.</b> For if she became defiled she shall die, and if she did not become defiled she shall be publicly disgraced, for she had the audacity to transgress her husband's warning and seclude herself."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:38:49.026066511Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}